KZ3 patch 2061 (RSX pass 62, porting-status step 9q): keyboard binds by key position, not by layout.
pad_keybinds.h: a binding code is the US-layout virtual key of a key POSITION; the 49 layout-dependent positions
(letters, digits, punctuation, the ISO Oem102 key) carry their PC/AT scancode (pad_kb_pos_keys). PadKbLayout
(pad_kb_layout_build, platform-free: the host passes scancode -> virtual key and scancode -> legend queries) maps
positions to the active layout's virtual keys for polling and to its legends for the Keyboard page
(pad_kb_key_short). Files written from now on carry "keys = positions"; a file without it is from before 2061 (its
names were the active layout's keys) and pad_kb_migrate rebinds each slot to the position that layout gives the key,
except inputs still on their old default pair, which take the default positions.
cellPad.c: MapVirtualKeyExW(MAPVK_VSC_TO_VK) + GetKeyNameTextW build the layout; rebuilt when the foreground
thread's HKL changes (read each focused poll: the switch WM_INPUTLANGCHANGE announces); GetAsyncKeyState polls the
translated keys; the one-time migration rewrites the file; pad_kb_key_label gives the keycaps the legend in the ANSI
code page (TextOutA). KZ3_KB_LAYOUT=<KLID> forces a layout (Windows checks). Log: [keybinds] layout ... positions
W A S D are ... here; [keybinds] ... migrated to key positions. Host test: tools/smoke/test_pad_keybinds.sh
(section 6, fake French AZERTY table).

